ace its aggressive against people of  color for no apparent reason but I think  the video of these events have allowed  for people to see the difference and  being a person of color and a white  person because most of us have been a  victim or have experienced some sort of  racism whether it be you know at a  restaurant at a department store you  know in school at your job and you not  tell people in 1998 as a you know lost  to a new lawyer I was the first woman  and person of color to be hired at my  law firm well I mean but my law school  class was only two percent  african-american if if 2 percent I think  it might have been class of 221 maybe 11  people of color and so you know even  though we have made strides there's a  lot of movement that needs to happen for  people of color I was gonna say kind of  on that note of share  entering a law firm experience do you  have a memory of the first time you  experienced racism as a little girl I  really didn't know if I thought racism  really existed until I was hired to do  some tutoring for a white family because  I've always been very intellectually  sound and the young boy said to his  friend sucessful I don't want anyone to  see my tutor because she's black and oh  I cried and I cried because I had never  heard anyone you know and he was  whispering it but I had never heard  anything that sounds so ridiculous  like I don't want someone to see my to  her because she's black and so that was  my first mom away I was like oh my gosh  people really have feelings about people  because they are black and I was just  tutor and I'm like you know why would  that be a problem why would you be  embarrassed by that you know so it yet  was my first you know experience with  you know that I obviously know it is  racist  thank you for sharing that thanks for  being so open and honest always  [Music]
 

